# Question: how much of a team's working day do interruptions eat, what does
# it cost a year, and how likely is it to be more than a quarter of the day?
#
# Run it (it uses the shared formulas):
#   ubc --scenario delivery/context-switching
# Change an assumption, for example a team with protected focus hours:
#   ubc --set 'interruptions = 1 to 4' --scenario delivery/context-switching
# See which assumption matters most:
#   ubc --sens lost_share --scenario delivery/context-switching
#
# Every "a to b" is a 90% confidence interval. Amounts are in euros.

# Assumptions
people = 6                        # engineers in the team
interruptions = 3 to 10           # interruptions per person a day: messages, questions, unplanned meetings
minutes_lost = 10 to 25           # to get back into the task; studies of office work report around 20
hours_per_day = 8                 # working hours in a day
salary = 50k to 80k               # gross yearly salary
overhead = 1.25 to 1.4            # taxes, benefits and equipment on top of the salary

# Calculation
lost_hours = interruptions * minutes_lost / 60               # hours a person loses a day
lost_share = lost_hours / hours_per_day                      # share of the working day
team_hours_week = lost_hours * people * 5                    # hours the whole team loses a week
yearly_cost = people * loaded_cost(salary, overhead) * lost_share   # what those hours cost a year

# Result
team_hours_week
yearly_cost
P(lost_share > 0.25)              # how likely do interruptions eat more than a quarter of the day?
